An election was held in [[Romania]] for the presidency of the [[Provisional Council of National Unity]] (CPUN) on 13 February 1990. [[Ion Iliescu]] was elected by the as the body's president — hence as [[acting (law)|acting]]/[[ad interim]] [[President of Romania]] — in a meeting held on 13 February 1990.<ref>{{cite web|language=Romanian|last=Stoicu|first=Andrei|date=February 13, 2010|title=Ion Iliescu, ales preşedinte al CPUN|url=https://jurnalul.ro/special-jurnalul/ion-iliescu-ales-presedinte-al-cpun-535777.html|work=Jurnalul|access-date=26 July 2021}}</ref> During that meeting, the CPUN also chose its ''Executive Office'' members. Nevertheless, the vote count was never published.

== Background ==

The CPUN was created on 9 February 1990 as a recomposition of the Council of the National Salvation Front (CFSN), with the inclusion of 112 [[List of political parties in Romania|political parties]] representatives (3 per each party),{{cn|date=July 2021}} 27 [[Romanian ethnic minority parties|national minorities representatives]], and 3 representatives of the former political convicts (besides 112 representatives of the [[National Salvation Front (Romania)|National Salvation Front]] or FSN for short, Romania's largest governing body during the early 1990s).<ref>{{cite web |url=http://civvic.ro/act?id=384 |title=Decret-lege privind Consiliul Provizoriu de Uniune Națională |website=civvic.ro |publisher=Civvic |access-date=July 26, 2021 |language=Romanian}}</ref> This body acted as an ad interim [[Unicameralism|single-chamber]] [[parliament]], until the [[1990 Romanian general election]], when it was replaced with an elected [[Bicameralism|two-chamber]] [[Parliament of Romania|parliament]].

